================================================================================
SUMMARY OF INTENT (NON-BINDING OVERVIEW; OPERATIVE TERMS FOLLOW IN SECTIONS 1-9)
================================================================================

Standard permissive licenses (MIT, Apache, BSD) and standard Open Source
copyleft licenses (GPL, AGPL) are not anti-capitalist: they allow investor-owned
corporations, financial institutions, cloud monopolies, and commercial AI
laboratories to extract uncompensated value from the intellectual commons, run
internal proprietary deployments, and train closed foundation models without
paying or reciprocating to the creators or the commons.

This License establishes a strict Copyfarleft dual regime:

  1. FREE FOR HUMAN INTELLIGENCE OUTSIDE CAPITALIST ENTERPRISE (COMMONS GRANT):
     Any natural person acting outside capitalist employment/enterprise, any
     student, educator, independent researcher, non-commercial academic or
     public-interest research group, charitable nonprofit, or democratically
     governed 100% worker-owned cooperative may freely read, compile, execute,
     verify, modify, teach, and share The Work — provided that all shared or
     network-served derivatives remain under this exact License with full
     machine-readable source disclosed (Strong Network Share-Alike).

  2. PAID LICENSE REQUIRED FOR CAPITALIST ENTITIES & COMMERCIAL / AI USE:
     Zero rights are granted under this License to any for-profit corporation,
     venture-backed or investor-owned business, hedge fund or trading firm,
     commercial cloud provider, commercial silicon vendor, or commercial AI
     laboratory. Capitalist Entities must purchase a written commercial license
     from Hyperactive Labs, Inc. before copying, compiling, running, evaluating,
     deploying, fabricating hardware from, or training AI models on The Work.

