OPERATIVE TERMS AND CONDITIONS
================================================================================

1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Licensor" means Hyperactive Labs, Inc. and Avik Jain, together with any
    successor or assign of their copyright and licensing authority.

1.2 "The Work" means all material distributed in or replicated from this
    repository or its content-addressed pool (`store/`), including without
    limitation all `.cub` and `.hypercubical` modules, C and assembly sources,
    interaction-net runtimes, typecheckers, compilers, lifters, formal proofs,
    mathematical and scientific derivations, RTL/GDSII silicon descriptions,
    web interfaces, documentation, essays, and content-addressed objects.

1.3 "Derivative Work" means any modification, translation, port, lowering,
    compilation, lifted or emitted code (including C, Rust, LLVM IR, x86-64,
    WASM, Verilog/RTL, or GDSII), linked system, or extension of the content-
    addressed pool that incorporates, adapts, or depends upon any protected
    expression of The Work.

1.4 "Commons Licensee" means exclusively:
    (a) a natural person acting strictly in an individual, personal, artistic,
        educational, or independent scientific capacity, outside the scope of
        any employment, consultancy, agency, or fiduciary duty for a Capitalist
        Entity;
    (b) a public school, public or non-profit university, or registered
        non-profit charitable/scientific organization (such as a U.S. IRC
        501(c)(3) organization or international equivalent) acting solely for
        non-commercial education, open scientific research, or non-commercial
        public service, provided no Capitalist Entity receives exclusive,
        proprietary, or preferential commercial rights in the resulting work;
    (c) a democratically governed worker-owned cooperative in which (i) 100%
        of voting governance and residual surplus belong to its worker-members
        on a one-worker-one-vote basis, (ii) zero equity, convertible debt
        carrying governance/royalty extraction, or profit participation is held
        by non-worker investors, and (iii) the cooperative does not employ
        non-member wage labor (other than a transparent, time-bounded
        probationary track of twelve months or less leading directly to full
        worker-membership); or
    (d) an unincorporated non-commercial collective or peer-to-peer commons
        operating without revenue extraction, investor ownership, or wage labor.

1.5 "Capitalist Entity" means any legal person, enterprise, organization, or
    arrangement that is not a Commons Licensee. Without limitation, "Capitalist
    Entity" includes every privately or publicly held for-profit corporation,
    limited liability company, partnership, venture-backed startup, sole
    proprietorship employing non-owner labor, bank, hedge fund, market maker,
    proprietary trading firm, asset manager, insurance company, defense or
    intelligence contractor, telecommunications or cloud operator, semiconductor
    company, and commercial AI or research laboratory (including any "capped-
    profit" entity, public-benefit corporation, or for-profit subsidiary or
    affiliate of a non-profit foundation).

1.6 "Capitalist or Commercial Use" means any reproduction, storage, compilation,
    execution, evaluation, benchmarking, internal research and development,
    internal tooling, production deployment, network or SaaS hosting, consulting
    delivery, financial/trading execution, hardware/FPGA/ASIC/GDSII synthesis
    or fabrication, or distribution of The Work or any Derivative Work:
    (a) by, at the direction of, or for the benefit of a Capitalist Entity;
    (b) by any employee, officer, founder, partner, contractor, or agent of a
        Capitalist Entity acting within the scope of their engagement or using
        equipment, cloud accounts, or funds of a Capitalist Entity; or
    (c) in exchange for commercial fees, subscriptions, licensing revenue,
        advertising, data monetization, financial trading return, or privately
        appropriated commercial advantage.

1.7 "AI & Automated Model Ingestion" means any scraping, copying, curation,
    tokenization, pre-training, continued training, fine-tuning, reinforcement
    learning, preference optimization, reward modeling, proof/trace harvesting,
    synthetic-data generation, knowledge distillation, embedding generation, or
    retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) performed on or using The Work or any
    output generated by executing The Work.

