3. STRONG NETWORK SHARE-ALIKE & ANTI-ENCLOSURE CONDITIONS

The grant in Section 2 is expressly conditioned on all of the following:

3.1 Same License Only (No Permissive Laundering). Every copy of The Work and
    every Derivative Work that you distribute, publish, replicate into a public
    content-addressed pool, or make available to any third party must be
    licensed as a whole under this exact License (or, at your option, a later
    version published by Licensor). You may not relicense The Work or any
    Derivative Work under MIT, BSD, Apache, GPL, AGPL, Creative Commons, or
    proprietary terms, nor impose additional restrictions on Commons Licensees.

3.2 Network & Peer-to-Peer Source Disclosure. If you modify The Work or create
    a Derivative Work (including extending `store/` modules, altering server or
    kernel behavior, or compiling specialized binaries/WASM/silicon) and enable
    users to interact with it remotely over any network (HTTP, WebSocket,
    WebRTC, P2P content-addressed sync, RPC, or remote proof checking), you must
    prominently provide every interacting user immediate, no-charge network
    access to download the complete corresponding machine-readable source text
    and content-addressed dependency closure under this License.

3.3 Preservation of Notices & Content Provenance. You must retain intact all
    copyright, authorship, attribution, cryptographic hash, and license notices
    in every source file, `README`, user interface footer, and replicated store
    manifest.

4. EXPRESS EXCLUSION OF CAPITALIST ENTITIES, COMMERCIAL USE & AI SCRAPING

4.1 Zero License to Capitalist Entities ("Pay to Touch"). THIS LICENSE GRANTS
    ZERO RIGHTS TO ANY CAPITALIST ENTITY AND ZERO RIGHTS FOR ANY CAPITALIST OR
    COMMERCIAL USE. Without a separate, written, fee-bearing commercial license
    agreement executed in advance by Hyperactive Labs, Inc., a Capitalist
    Entity has no permission under copyright, patent, or applicable law to
    clone, download, store, copy, compile, execute, test, benchmark, link,
    modify, deploy, host, synthesize hardware from, or otherwise use The Work
    in whole or in part — including strictly internal corporate R&D, evaluation,
    or employee use on corporate systems.

4.2 Prohibition on Unlicensed AI Training & Distillation.
    (a) Capitalist Entities and commercial AI laboratories are strictly
        prohibited from performing any AI & Automated Model Ingestion (Section
        1.7) on The Work without an executed paid AI Licensing Agreement with
        Hyperactive Labs, Inc. Presence of The Work in a publicly readable git
        repository or decentralized web seed constitutes publication for human
        and Commons inspection ONLY and explicitly opts out of all statutory or
        implied text-and-data-mining (TDM) exceptions to the maximum extent
        permitted by law (including EU Directive 2019/790 Article 4(3)).
    (b) A Commons Licensee may perform AI & Automated Model Ingestion on The
        Work solely to train or evaluate a non-commercial model whose complete
        weights, training code, and training manifest are publicly released
        under an anti-capitalist commons license no less protective against
        commercial capture than this License.

4.3 Anti-Circumvention. No Capitalist Entity may circumvent Section 4.1 or 4.2
    by acting through an individual employee's personal account, an independent
    contractor, a university lab, a non-profit wrapper, or an affiliate. Any
    upstream contribution voluntarily submitted to this repository by a third
    party is provided under this License and grants Licensor the non-exclusive
    right to include that contribution in both Commons and commercial releases,
    unless expressly marked otherwise at submission.

